UID:8fhjoenxiyg3PE2MtM4st
SUMMARY:Unexpected Routes: Refugee Writers in Mexico
DTSTAMP:20260821T033714Z
DTSTART:20260924T183000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Holocaust Museum Houston for an evening lecture featuring 
	Dr. Tabea Linhard\, author of Unexpected Routes: Refugee Writers in Mexico
	. \nUnexpected Routes chronicles the refugee journeys of six writers whose
	 lives were upended by fascism in the aftermath of the Spanish Civil War a
	nd during World War II. During her lecture\, Dr. Linhard will explore the 
	stories of German author Ruth Rewald\, who was murdered during the Holocau
	st\, and Czech writer and journalist Egon Erwin Kisch\, who wrote about th
	e Holocaust while in Mexico. While the writers she discusses in the book c
	ame from different backgrounds and wrote in different languages\, they all
	 made sense of their forced displacement in works that reveal their confli
	cted relationships with the people and places they encountered in transit 
	as well as in Mexico. The literary output of these brilliant\, prolific\, 
	but also flawed individuals reflects the most salient contradictions of wh
	at it meant to escape from fascistoccupied Europe. \nThis event is free an
	d open to the public but advanced registration is required.\n\nhttps://hmh
	.org/event/unexpected-routes-refugee-writers-in-mexico/\n\nFrom Holocaust 
	Museum Houston
URL:https://hmh.org/event/unexpected-routes-refugee-writers-in-mexico/
LOCATION:Albert and Ethel Herzstein Theater
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:holocaust-museum-houston
CATEGORIES:Holocaust Museum Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
